NON-BLOCKING PRECISION NOTES (facts for the lead; neither is a false statement and
neither fails a criterion as written):
  (i) For a symlinked DIRECTORY, the spot-check shows os.ReadFile returns
      "is a directory" (EISDIR). In buildZip that error is returned from the walk fn
      and aborts the snapshot (snapshot.go:197-200, then 214-216). The comment says
      only that such a directory's "contents are not walked here" -- true, and it makes
      no claim that the snapshot succeeds -- but it is silent on the abort.
  (ii) "a symlinked file is read through by os.ReadFile below" elides the
      `if skip(path, false) { return nil }` at snapshot.go:187, which sits between the
      walk visit and the ReadFile; a symlinked file matching the skip predicate is not
      read. The comment carries no "always", so this is an elision, not an overclaim.
